  "findings": [
    "P1-empty-stripe: The new empty-line branch discards a Java space atom while Rust still emits an empty text element. Last baseline remains unchanged but canvas is shortened. Actor Java232/before234/after227; boundary Java204/before206/after199. Next repair: Port StripeSimple empty-stripe atom behavior and include every emitted UText baseline in the painted union. Do not subtract a font-specific correction.",
    "P1-boundary-shadow-input: USymbolBoundary.getDrawing converts nonzero Fashion shadow to4; Rust helper consumes raw18 and its existing boundary emitter omits both shadow filters. Java106x170, before106x172, after117x193. The actor raw-shadow control passes, proving the policies differ by symbol. Next repair: Apply the Boundary symbol factory shadow policy before measurement/drawing, propagate that same Fashion to path/ellipse emission, then measure their distinct LimitFinder extrema.",
    "P1-emitted-text-max: The estimator uses a fixed plain-font line advance and one anchor ascent. emit_text emits shifted subscript runs; Java Sea/AtomText uses actual per-stripe dimensions/positions. actor_sized emitted Rust final baseline209.5117 gives max211.0117, but after canvas222 fails even its own expected envelope226; Java final baseline221.1777/canvas237. Both preferred-height and painted-run dependencies remain. Next repair: Keep preferred dimensions and painted bounds as separate results of a common positioned text/symbol model. Union actual run baselines after markup offsets; route prerequisite shared text/model repairs separately, without doing them in this review.",
    "P2-stereotype-style: Java inherits bold FontStyle for stereotype; Rust retains italic and narrower measurement. Only the stereotype node differs in these controls. Next repair: Resolve/measure/emit the actual stereotype style from EntityImageDescription styleStereo; preserve label styling independently.",
    "P2-degenerate-residue: Actor preferred-size degenerate control has an existing position/stereotype residual; before/after bytes are identical. Boundary degenerate passes. This is outside the new non-degenerated-max computation and is retained without claiming a fix. Next repair: Investigate the degenerate actor/stereotype model separately; do not alter the preserved exception to disguise this residual."
